                <pb facs="0337" n="225" sameAs="frus:frus1919Russia/pg225"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">861.00/5681: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Russia</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Tenney</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1919-11-17T10:00:00+08:00"><hi rendition="#italic">November 17,
                                1919, 10 a.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received November 18, 3:05
                        a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>[From Harris at Novo Nikolaievsk:]</p>
                <p>Omsk fell 7 o’clock evening November 15th. Bolsheviki now thirteen versts east of
                    Omsk. Great bridge over Irtysh River at Omsk destroyed by retreating Siberian
                    Army. Kolchak at Barabinsk. Gold still
                    safe. Japanese mission with Ambassador Kato approaching Novo Nikolaievsk.
                        General Janin leaving Novo
                    Nikolaievsk for Irkutsk morning of 18th. I am also leaving for Irkutsk at the
                    same time. Harris.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                        >Tenney</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
